WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:04.980
Faceless One

00:07.440 --> 00:13.700
Satsuki Kazuma and his family were murdered.

00:13.700 --> 00:16.990
I will now tell how.

00:18.200 --> 00:21.120
The culprit is the late Kazuma’s wife, Chou.

00:21.540 --> 00:25.790
For her crime, she was incarcerated immediately.

00:52.940 --> 00:54.780
That’s much better.

00:59.120 --> 01:01.700
I accept responsibility for my crime.

01:01.870 --> 01:04.960
Part the First

01:29.400 --> 01:33.730
The blue moon illuminated

01:33.780 --> 01:37.700
your wandering shadow.

01:38.320 --> 01:42.200
I could never tell you all I wanted to say.

01:42.200 --> 01:47.120
It was so very frustrating.

01:47.210 --> 01:51.000
I think about your faked smile,

01:51.590 --> 01:55.630
and forget all the hot tears we shed.

01:56.090 --> 01:58.300
What do these empty husks,

01:58.340 --> 02:04.140
those empty eyes of yours, reflect, my dear?

02:04.890 --> 02:09.350
The transient quarter moon

02:09.730 --> 02:11.520
hides in a rift in the clouds,

02:11.480 --> 02:13.900
as darkness seeps up from the ground.

02:13.940 --> 02:18.360
Tell me the truth, please.

02:18.700 --> 02:20.530
Are you so despondent

02:20.610 --> 02:24.990
that you still sit alone, sighing?

02:25.370 --> 02:27.870
And so, the case is solved!

02:32.750 --> 02:33.960
Just what

02:36.210 --> 02:37.920
did you do?

02:41.300 --> 02:42.390
Who are you?

02:42.680 --> 02:46.850
As you’ve likely surmised, I am a fellow prisoner.

02:46.850 --> 02:49.600
I am a medicine seller by trade.

02:50.020 --> 02:53.310
I had a rather rude customer, you see.

02:53.770 --> 02:56.440
He said that the pills I sold him did nothing for his condition.

02:56.440 --> 02:59.280
He came at me with accusations of fraud and the like.

03:00.530 --> 03:06.490
Personally, the very belief that medicine alone
can cure one’s ailments does not sit well with me.

03:06.490 --> 03:10.210
An ineffective medicine is
rendered such by one’s own lack of belief.

03:10.210 --> 03:13.330
They are held together by a common
thread, like sardines hung out to dry.

03:13.670 --> 03:17.800
When I told him that, though, he
screamed at me to return his money.

03:17.800 --> 03:20.050
That’s when the authorities arrived on the scene.

03:20.470 --> 03:25.010
I’m most embarrassed that a
customer should put me in such a situation.

03:25.010 --> 03:28.770
Wait, or are sardines dried on sticks?

03:30.520 --> 03:32.100
This is quite odd.

03:32.810 --> 03:34.940
Don’t you think?

03:34.940 --> 03:37.480
After all,

03:37.480 --> 03:40.240
a man and woman should not share the same cell.

03:40.240 --> 03:42.990
Well, well, at any rate

03:44.570 --> 03:46.330
you’re set to die.

03:48.080 --> 03:50.040
So you knew.

03:50.040 --> 03:50.540
Oh,

03:51.160 --> 03:53.250
well yes.

03:53.250 --> 03:57.000
The populace is abuzz with rumors of your crime.

03:57.000 --> 04:02.430
Ochou, the devil-woman who killed a samurai’s entire
house, including her own husband and father-in-law.

04:03.510 --> 04:05.180
Is that so?

04:05.180 --> 04:07.850
Is that how they refer to me, then?

04:08.350 --> 04:14.730
Still, it was a rather heinous crime.

04:19.480 --> 04:22.650
Four people hung from a plum tree.

04:22.650 --> 04:24.160
That wasn’t how it happened.

04:24.160 --> 04:26.990
Oh, really?

04:26.990 --> 04:27.870
Well, then.

04:31.910 --> 04:34.250
What a dreadful fate.

04:35.210 --> 04:36.920
That’s wrong, as well.

04:37.540 --> 04:40.420
Is it, now?

04:40.420 --> 04:42.340
Then how did it happen?

04:49.260 --> 04:49.890
Hm?

04:49.890 --> 04:52.180
Is something the matter?

04:52.180 --> 04:54.730
Oh, well, I’ve forgotten.

04:54.730 --> 04:56.900
Oh, forgotten, have you?

04:57.810 --> 05:02.940
Well, rumors develop quickly indeed.

05:02.940 --> 05:05.360
How you did it is irrelevant.

05:05.780 --> 05:10.780
Cooked in miso or cured with salt, a fish is a fish, you see.

05:10.780 --> 05:12.370
You make no sense at all.

05:12.700 --> 05:17.790
I cannot believe a woman could do this alone, is my point.

05:17.790 --> 05:19.340
What is that?

05:19.340 --> 05:20.840
A scale.

05:20.840 --> 05:21.750
A scale?

05:22.380 --> 05:24.800
Pay it no heed.

05:24.800 --> 05:28.010
It is merely a tool for my trade.

05:32.140 --> 05:40.110
There were no witnesses and no physical
evidence, just your own admission of guilt.

05:40.110 --> 05:42.860
All the details are quite vague.

05:42.860 --> 05:45.530
Truth be told, Ochou-san,

05:45.530 --> 05:50.530
I do not believe that you acted alone.

05:57.000 --> 06:02.210
I think that it was the work of a Mononoke.

06:02.210 --> 06:03.170
Mononoke?

06:03.670 --> 06:07.300
Does that ring any bells with you?

06:07.760 --> 06:09.340
No, none at all.

06:09.340 --> 06:10.550
No, none at all.

06:12.260 --> 06:15.270
I did it by myself.

06:15.560 --> 06:17.560
I see.

06:17.560 --> 06:19.480
But you know…

06:19.480 --> 06:20.270
Yes?

06:20.270 --> 06:29.320
Well, you understand, people
always have a certain air about them.

06:29.320 --> 06:31.240
A certain expression.

06:31.240 --> 06:31.950
Expression.

06:32.580 --> 06:38.330
You do not seem like a woman
bound for the gallows in the morning.

06:38.330 --> 06:39.870
That is what I mean.

06:40.330 --> 06:43.750
Well, my white kimono distinguishes me as such.

06:43.750 --> 06:46.710
Your jailor determines how you dress.

06:47.090 --> 06:49.510
Your face is of more concern to me than your garb.

06:49.510 --> 06:54.680
What I’m trying to say is that you seem an
entirely different person from the normal Ochou-san.

06:55.100 --> 06:57.180
Whatever do you mean?

06:57.180 --> 06:59.480
You could not possibly know how
I act under normal circumstances.

07:00.730 --> 07:04.320
Just who are you?

07:07.900 --> 07:09.700
Who are you?

07:10.610 --> 07:12.160
Answer me.

07:12.160 --> 07:14.580
Who are you?

07:14.580 --> 07:17.120
Just a simple medicine seller.

07:17.120 --> 07:19.790
Actually, I’m a criminal right now.

07:19.790 --> 07:21.500
What are you doing here?

07:23.130 --> 07:24.340
Answer me.

07:24.340 --> 07:26.550
How did you get in here?

07:26.550 --> 07:28.260
Amazing it can speak.

07:28.260 --> 07:32.130
This is the first time I’ve met this sort of Mononoke.

07:32.590 --> 07:35.100
Oh, don’t be stupid.

07:35.100 --> 07:37.970
He isn’t anything strange like that.

07:37.970 --> 07:39.480
You must not leave.

07:39.480 --> 07:40.480
Please move.

07:40.770 --> 07:42.230
You must not leave.

07:42.650 --> 07:44.150
What are you doing?

07:44.150 --> 07:45.610
Let me go!

07:45.610 --> 07:46.940
Please, let me go!

07:46.940 --> 07:48.440
Let me go!

07:48.440 --> 07:50.360
Why are you getting in my way?

07:50.740 --> 07:52.070
You must not leave.

07:52.070 --> 07:56.740
You are safe as long as you stay in here.

07:56.740 --> 07:57.370
What?

08:04.290 --> 08:05.960
You’re most suspicious.

08:05.960 --> 08:07.420
Who are you?

08:09.510 --> 08:13.470
As I thought, she was possessed.

08:13.470 --> 08:18.850
It was my belief, though, that I would
have to break those bars to reveal your Form.

08:24.520 --> 08:26.110
I never thought

08:26.900 --> 08:28.230
that you would

08:29.230 --> 08:31.240
come

08:31.610 --> 08:32.700
to me.

08:34.530 --> 08:36.530
Witness the Form.

08:37.120 --> 08:38.700
What?

08:38.700 --> 08:42.580
You aren’t a Mononoke’s true Form?

08:44.420 --> 08:46.000
Whatever do you mean?

08:46.000 --> 08:48.380
Why are you getting in my way?

08:48.670 --> 08:50.380
You must not leave.

08:50.380 --> 08:52.590
You will be safe as long as you stay in here.

08:52.590 --> 08:55.840
If you believe this place holds you, it is a prison.

08:55.840 --> 08:58.800
If you do not wish to leave, it will become a fortress.

08:55.840 --> 08:57.140
What do you mean?

08:59.560 --> 09:03.810
Do you wish to return to that place again?

09:03.810 --> 09:05.690
Return?

09:17.820 --> 09:19.280
I do not mind.

09:21.370 --> 09:24.160
Mankind is far more frightening.

09:24.160 --> 09:25.870
I do not mind.

09:25.870 --> 09:28.880
Surely there must be kind Mononoke.

09:29.290 --> 09:31.300
Did you hear what she said?

09:31.920 --> 09:35.300
Infinite providence lies with me!

09:46.730 --> 09:50.650
Wander now, in search of your Form.

09:59.570 --> 10:01.830
We should be safe here.

10:01.830 --> 10:03.950
They won’t follow us for a while.

10:03.950 --> 10:05.750
Who are you?

10:05.750 --> 10:11.130
All the ridiculous rumors must have shocked you.

10:11.130 --> 10:15.170
As that man said, I am a Mononoke.

10:15.170 --> 10:16.840
Mononoke?

10:16.840 --> 10:21.220
I was born to free you from prison.

10:22.930 --> 10:23.890
Prison?

10:37.860 --> 10:39.820
Prison?

10:43.280 --> 10:44.580
Sake! Sake!

10:44.580 --> 10:46.330
I need more sake!

10:49.710 --> 10:53.380
I told you to bring me more sake! What are you doing?

10:53.380 --> 10:56.380
I—I’m sorry!

10:56.380 --> 11:00.340
Ochou-san, just get us some more sake!

11:00.340 --> 11:02.890
What a worthless wife you have.

11:03.640 --> 11:05.470
A lazy girl, indeed.

11:05.470 --> 11:09.020
Brother, whyever did you take her in?

11:09.020 --> 11:13.060
Her mother begged me to.

11:13.060 --> 11:18.940
If your first wife hadn’t hung herself, would
you ever have accepted her into your home?

11:18.940 --> 11:21.410
Well, she’s a pretty good cook,

11:21.410 --> 11:24.620
and good in bed, too!

11:24.620 --> 11:27.160
Oh stop, you’re just terrible!

11:48.470 --> 11:50.140
Your heart

11:53.770 --> 11:57.860
wished to purge itself of the rage
that was building up like a poison.

11:57.860 --> 11:59.150
Poison?

11:59.150 --> 12:02.990
Perhaps you thing it strange to
hear a Mononoke speak of poison.

12:05.160 --> 12:06.530
Not at all.

12:09.370 --> 12:10.950
That sensation…

12:16.840 --> 12:20.380
Thanks to that sensation, I was able to stand it.

12:26.640 --> 12:33.140
Over and over and over again, you saved me.

12:33.140 --> 12:35.810
Must we return?

12:35.810 --> 12:38.070
Indeed, we must.

12:38.400 --> 12:40.440
My power is limited.

12:40.440 --> 12:42.990
We will soon be pursued.

12:42.990 --> 12:44.110
Come.

12:49.660 --> 12:50.540
No.

12:51.200 --> 12:53.330
I do not want to go back there.

12:53.790 --> 12:56.290
You are set to be hung.

12:56.290 --> 13:01.090
Your appeals are exhausted.
You are truly on the brink of death.

13:01.090 --> 13:03.300
If I go back there…

13:03.300 --> 13:07.050
It’s all the same, whether I stay or go.

13:07.050 --> 13:10.260
If you do not return, you will be
running from your crime all your life.

13:10.260 --> 13:11.430
So be it.

13:11.430 --> 13:14.310
If you are found, you will be executed on the spot.

13:14.310 --> 13:16.270
That would be easier, I’m sure.

13:18.310 --> 13:20.400
The man in the prison?

13:21.860 --> 13:24.360
Was it that man who put such thoughts in your head?

13:25.990 --> 13:28.530
I simply do not wish to return.

13:44.130 --> 13:45.630
Ochou-san.

13:45.630 --> 13:46.800
Yes?

13:46.800 --> 13:49.140
Will you marry me?

13:50.300 --> 13:51.640
But you’re…

13:51.640 --> 13:53.680
Indeed, I am not human.

13:53.680 --> 13:57.940
However, I do hold Shape and Form similar to that of a man.

13:58.690 --> 14:01.270
I cannot remove my mask,

14:01.270 --> 14:06.990
but I can sing and dance and do
everything necessary to provide for you.

14:07.860 --> 14:09.780
Please, be my wife!

14:15.700 --> 14:17.620
Are you certain you want me?

14:18.870 --> 14:21.710
You want a convicted criminal as a wife?

14:22.170 --> 14:23.590
I want you.

14:29.340 --> 14:31.720
Does that mean you accept?

14:33.430 --> 14:36.020
Yes! Yes!

14:36.020 --> 14:37.140
Yes!

14:37.140 --> 14:38.600
Oh, yes!

14:39.940 --> 14:41.190
Yes.

14:41.980 --> 14:43.940
Let us be wed immediately!

15:01.710 --> 15:04.960
Ochou, today we start our new lives.

15:06.920 --> 15:08.300
Yes.

15:08.300 --> 15:11.760
Everyone, look! This is my bride!

15:11.760 --> 15:13.470
Look at my beautiful Ochou-san!

15:13.470 --> 15:17.220
I’m astounded that Ochou-san agreed to marry you.

15:17.220 --> 15:19.390
I’m so jealous! So jealous!

15:19.390 --> 15:21.020
Congratulations! Congratulations!

15:21.020 --> 15:24.190
Congratulations! Congratulations!

15:28.530 --> 15:31.450
Oh my, they’re such a rowdy bunch.

15:31.450 --> 15:33.490
They’re all so nice.

15:33.490 --> 15:36.280
They’ve always been around you.

15:36.280 --> 15:37.580
Really?

15:37.580 --> 15:39.330
You simply did not notice them.

15:39.660 --> 15:43.080
So jealous! So jealous!

15:40.580 --> 15:44.540
They have all protected you.

15:43.080 --> 15:46.460
Congratulations! Congratulations!

15:44.540 --> 15:50.170
People tend to forget how many people they have met,

15:50.170 --> 15:55.220
and how many of them have helped them.

15:55.220 --> 15:56.970
From now on, though, it will be different.

15:58.430 --> 16:04.100
From now on, I will be your reason for living!

16:07.230 --> 16:08.690
Yes.

16:22.580 --> 16:24.500
Our vows are completed.

16:25.540 --> 16:28.380
We two are now as one.

16:28.380 --> 16:29.630
Yes.

16:39.760 --> 16:43.560
I hid myself, so as not to interrupt your taking of vows.

16:44.100 --> 16:47.060
I merely wish to express my
gratitude and extend my best wishes.

16:47.560 --> 16:49.650
Who are you?

16:49.650 --> 16:53.070
Thank you. Thank you so much.

16:53.070 --> 16:54.530
Mother?

16:54.530 --> 16:55.070
What?

16:55.070 --> 16:56.160
Mother?

16:59.870 --> 17:02.660
What? What is this?

17:08.170 --> 17:10.710
It is changing for me.

17:10.710 --> 17:12.920
What?

17:12.920 --> 17:20.140
Now I can finally hold my head high as I visit
the graves of my ancestors, the Umezawake clan.

17:20.140 --> 17:22.430
Yes, you two.

17:22.430 --> 17:23.930
should really pay your respects.

17:25.640 --> 17:29.150
You were born exceptionally beautiful.

17:29.150 --> 17:32.440
Mind your appearance carefully,

17:32.440 --> 17:38.370
and you will be able to marry into a wealthy
family, in spite of your humble upbringing.

17:39.240 --> 17:41.080
Yes, Mother!

17:41.080 --> 17:44.160
Good girl. Good girl.

17:44.160 --> 17:46.120
Stop it! You must not show me that!

18:15.110 --> 18:16.150
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

18:16.150 --> 18:17.240
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

18:17.240 --> 18:18.150
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

18:18.150 --> 18:19.110
Yes, yes, yes, yes.

18:19.110 --> 18:20.780
Congratulations! Congratulations!

18:21.530 --> 18:24.160
That was quite a wonderful play.

18:24.160 --> 18:26.910
I enjoyed it very much.

18:27.660 --> 18:29.370
What happened to your face?

18:29.370 --> 18:31.750
My face?

18:33.460 --> 18:37.590
The character for “face” can also be read as “exterior.”

18:39.760 --> 18:45.640
The human face is nothing more than its exterior appearance.

18:45.640 --> 18:52.730
If I accept this face, it is quite easy to make it my own.

18:55.230 --> 18:57.900
Oh my, I see your mask has changed yet again.

19:03.280 --> 19:05.950
But where is your real face?

19:28.060 --> 19:29.980
Where did that come from?

19:46.160 --> 19:47.080
Darling!

20:01.970 --> 20:03.390
It’s collapsing.

20:05.800 --> 20:11.850
This new life I’d finally gained…

20:13.310 --> 20:15.690
It’s collapsing.

20:15.690 --> 20:17.730
This is a fake.

20:17.730 --> 20:22.860
It was all a play the Mononoke created to deceive you.

20:22.860 --> 20:24.160
Why?

20:24.780 --> 20:27.410
I thought he saved me.

20:27.990 --> 20:33.750
He must be hiding something.
Something he needed you not to notice.

20:34.370 --> 20:36.330
He wears a mask to hide his face.

20:36.960 --> 20:44.300
What is he hiding from you, that he required such a play?

20:44.840 --> 20:46.470
No…

20:49.100 --> 20:52.180
You who have forgotten your face,

20:52.180 --> 20:54.350
Mononoke,

20:59.480 --> 21:01.940
show me your Form.

21:01.940 --> 21:03.150
show me your Form.

21:07.570 --> 21:10.030
To be continued

21:11.910 --> 21:19.420
Without you, I just can’t smile.

21:20.550 --> 21:30.470
I walk this banal town,

21:30.470 --> 21:36.560
feeling such intense emotions.

21:37.100 --> 21:42.940
I know that if I could treasure them and live on,

21:43.030 --> 21:52.240
I would need nothing else.

21:52.910 --> 22:00.420
The summer flowers that bloomed in the sky

22:00.420 --> 22:06.720
Come falling down, dancing in the wind.

22:06.800 --> 22:10.050
I can barely recall the night sky

22:10.050 --> 22:13.350
where they all came tumbling down,

22:13.350 --> 22:24.190
so what I can still recall is all the more precious.
